    "<div style=\"font-family:'Times New Roman'; color:blue; font-size:20px;\">\n",
    "\n",
    "<h1 style=\"color:red; font-size:22px;\"> Transit Demand Prediction using Machine Learning</h1>\n",
    "\n",
    "<p>\n",
    "This project focuses on predicting transit demand (number of passengers or transportation usage) using various machine learning algorithms. \n",
    "The goal is to help urban planners and transportation authorities efficiently manage resources, optimize schedules, and improve public transport accessibility.\n",
    "</p>\n",
    "\n",
    "<h2 style=\"color:red; font-size:22px;\"> Motivation</h2>\n",
    "\n",
    "<p>\n",
    "Public transportation systems are essential for urban mobility. However, unpredictable fluctuations in demand often lead to overcrowding or underutilized services. \n",
    "By developing an intelligent model that predicts demand based on factors like time, weather, population, and location, \n",
    "this project aims to enhance decision-making and promote smart city initiatives.\n",
    "</p>\n",
    "\n",
    "<h2 style=\"color:red; font-size:22px;\">⚙️ Development Lifecycle of the App</h2>\n",
    "\n",
    "<p>\n",
    "The entire development lifecycle consists of several key phases:\n",
    "</p>\n",
    "\n",
    "<ol style=\"color:blue;\">\n",
    "  <li><b>Data Collection:</b> Synthetic data generation for transit demand parameters such as distance, temperature, weekday/weekend indicators, etc.</li>\n",
    "  <li><b>Data Preprocessing:</b> Handling missing values, normalization using <code>StandardScaler</code>, and splitting into training and testing sets.</li>\n",
    "  <li><b>Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA):</b> Visualizing correlations, feature importance, and understanding variable impact.</li>\n",
    "  <li><b>Model Training:</b> Models such as Linear Regression, Random Forest Regressor, Gradient Boosting Regressor, and XGBoost Regressor were used.</li>\n",
    "  <li><b>Hyperparameter Tuning:</b> Using <code>GridSearchCV</code> for optimal model parameters to improve accuracy.</li>\n",
    "  <li><b>Cross Validation:</b> Evaluating each model’s performance across multiple folds for better reliability.</li>\n",
    "  <li><b>Model Saving:</b> The best model and scaler were saved using <code>joblib</code> for deployment purposes.</li>\n",
    "</ol>\n",
    "\n",
    "<h2 style=\"color:red; font-size:22px;\"> Installation</h2>\n",
    "\n",
    "<p>\n",
    "To run this project locally, follow these steps:\n",
    "</p>\n",
    "\n",
    "<pre style=\"background-color:#f5f5f5; padding:10px; border-radius:8px;\">\n",
    "# Clone the repository\n",
    "git clone https://github.com/YourUsername/Transit-Demand-Prediction.git\n",
    "\n",
    "# Navigate to the project directory\n",
    "cd Transit-Demand-Prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "# Install the required dependencies\n",
    "pip install -r requirements.txt\n",
    "\n",
    "# Launch Jupyter Notebook\n",
    "jupyter notebook\n",
    "</pre>\n",
    "\n",
    "<h2 style=\"color:red; font-size:22px;\"> Languages and Libraries Used</h2>\n",
    "\n",
    "<ul style=\"color:blue;\">\n",
    "  <li><b>Programming Language:</b> Python</li>\n",
    "  <li><b>Libraries:</b> Pandas, NumPy, Scikit-learn, XGBoost, Matplotlib, Seaborn, Joblib</li>\n",
    "  <li><b>Development Tool:</b> Jupyter Notebook</li>\n",
    "</ul>\n",
    "\n",
    "<h2 style=\"color:red; font-size:22px;\"> Results</h2>\n",
    "\n",
    "<p>\n",
    "After model training and evaluation, the best-performing model was found to be <b>XGBoost Regressor</b>, \n",
    "providing the highest R² score and lowest mean absolute error. \n",
    "The final model was saved as <b>best_transit_model.pkl</b> and the scaler as <b>scaler.pkl</b>.\n",
    "</p>\n",
    "\n",
    "<h2 style=\"color:red; font-size:22px;\"> Conclusion</h2>\n",
    "\n",
    "<p>\n",
    "This project demonstrates how machine learning can revolutionize transportation systems through demand forecasting. \n",
    "It serves as a prototype for smart city transportation planning and can be extended using real-world data for production deployment.\n",
    "</p>\n",
    "\n",
    "</div>\n"
